mfletche@sun1.iusb.indiana.edu (Mike Fletcher) writes:

>Shopkeepers:
>  Can they be polymorphed?  Everytime I try they just break out and attack me.
>  Can you actually kill one?

Of course you can. Just make sure you have LOTS of hit points, and a
good AC. That's what THEY have as well (your stats are your starting
stats):

Stat	You	Shopkeeper	Remarks
~~~~~~	~~~	~~~~~~~~~~	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Level	1	12		determines HP
Move	10	18		if you don't have intrinsic speed
AC	10	0		if you don't have armour
MagRes	0	50
Damage	1d6	4d4, 4d4	assuming non-weapon combat

A shopkeeper cannot be polymorphed, and can use magical objects.

Let's say that you should be around level 10 with a decent armour class
before even thinking of taking on a shopkeeper.

>Enchanting Armour and Weapons:
>  I had a +7 or +8 Athame on a Wizard and I read one more blessed Enchant 
>    Weapon and it shuttered and dissapeared... After this I noticed I had an
>    extra few points of strength (from 18/03 - 18/12) -- This also happened
>    to my +5 shield when I read a uncursed Enchant Armour -- What happens
>    to these items?

You should NEVER enchant a weapon or armour too high. They can only
take a fair amount of enchantment. If your weapon is already at +5 or
higher, there is a 2/3 chance that your weapon will evaporate. About
the same goes for armour: it can be safely enchanted up to +3, after
which point is has a 1-in-(current enchantment) chance of evaporating.
Elven armour can be enchanted up to +5 safely, and will warn you when
it is reaching this limit. Other armour can also warn you, with a
1-in-7 chance. So, if you managed to get your athame up to +7 and your
shield to +5, you already were very lucky indeed!

>Alignments and Gods:
> I would like someone to fill me in on switching religions after your god
> decides to hate you for no reason, or how to appease him enough to grant
> you items... I can make him happy enough to give me 1 artifact then he
> just ignores me the rest of the game it seems like.

After you've prayed, and been given something, it may take up to 3000
turns until you may pray again, depending on a lot of factors, which I
don't feel like explaining (I tried last week, and failed). Changing
alignment can be done by offering a unicorn of your alignment on
another god's altar. Making YOUR god happy again can be done by just
waiting (eventually, he will be happy with you again), or by offering a
lot on a co-aligned altar.

> Is there a spot where there will Always be an altar? I know there is one in 
> Gnomish mines... any others? (luckstones too...)

Both can only be found FOR SURE in the Gnomish Mines (town level,
bottom of the Mines, respectively).

>  Can I switch a non-aligned alter to my Gods alignment?

I believe you can, and I am SURE you can convert a non-co-aligned altar
to your alignment.

>Wormtooth:
>  What do I do with a blessed Wormtooth?

You might enchant it. It is a weapon. It will change into a crysknife
when you do enchant it, and will convert back to a worm tooth in case
you drop it. It's one of the best non-artifact weapons when enchanted.


